vices Missions & Chaplain Services PUC Church Records SERVE - Survivor Empowerment, Response to Violence, and Education Service Learning Student Finance Student & Spiritual Life Student Success Center Student Wellness Center | Counseling Services Student Wellness Center | Health Services Title IX Community Recreation Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Assistant or Associate or Full Professor of Accounting Applications are available in the Human Resources Office or available online . Applications from current employees are welcome. Applicants must be members of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. Email ( hr@puc.edu ), fax (707-965-6400), or mail (Human Resources Office, One Angwin Avenue, Angwin, CA 94508), your signed application to Human Resources Please contact Human Resources regarding questions about this position. Applications from qualified applicants are forwarded to the employing department by Human Resources Applicants selected for interviews will be contacted by Human Resources or the employing department Apply for job Start Date Upon receipt of qualified candidate Job Type Faculty Job Opening Department Business Administration Position Type Full Time Tenure Track Yes Job Summary The Business Administration faculty member teaches Accounting courses, supports student engagement, and provides academic advising.  This role includes contributing to departmental activities, participating in shared governance, and fostering a student-centered, close-knit academic community while maintaining positive community relationships. Desirable Qualifications Teaching experience is strongly preferred, particularly in-person instruction at the undergraduate or graduate level. Experience with online education will also reflect positively. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to engage positively and collaboratively with students and colleagues in support of the Pacific Union College mission. In lieu of a terminal degree in Accounting, candidates with a Master’s degree in Business Administration or Accounting combined with active professional certification or licensure or significant relevant professional experience will also be considered. Ability to integrate practical experience in engaging, student-centered instruction is highly valued. Compensation Salary; $54,382 - $76,314 (plus denominational benefits, depending upon qualifications and experience) Full Job Description View Full Job Description Application Deadline Applications will be reviewed as received. The position will remain open until it is filled. Apply for job PACIFIC UNION COLLEGE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER. Questions? Contact Human Resources Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Campus Map (800) 862-7080 (707) 965-6313 Apply Give Contact Visit Careers Academics Useful Links Information Academic Departments Bookstore Calendar Campus Map Consumer Information Directory Disability Services Discrimination Policy Emergency Info Library News Online Programs Pay Student Bill Photo Gallery Privacy Policy PUC CARES Act Grant Records Office Student Planning Title IX Information For Who Are You? Current Students New Students Future Students Transfer Students Parents & Families Alumni Visitors Faculty & Staff Veterans © Copyright 2026. Pacific Union College. All Rights reserved. | Privacy policy"
