ds SERVE - Survivor Empowerment, Response to Violence, and Education Service Learning Student Finance Student & Spiritual Life Student Success Center Student Wellness Center | Counseling Services Student Wellness Center | Health Services Title IX Community Recreation Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Adjunct Clinical Nursing Instructor Applications are available in the Human Resources Office or available online . Applications from current employees are welcome. Applicants must be members of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. Email ( hr@puc.edu ), fax (707-965-6400), or mail (Human Resources Office, One Angwin Avenue, Angwin, CA 94508), your signed application to Human Resources Please contact Human Resources regarding questions about this position. Applications from qualified applicants are forwarded to the employing department by Human Resources Applicants selected for interviews will be contacted by Human Resources or the employing department Apply for job Start Date Upon receipt of qualified candidate Job Type Staff Job Opening Department Nursing and Emergency Management Position Type Full Time Tenure Track No Job Summary An adjunct nursing instructor is a Registered Nurse with educational preparation and expertise in a specific area of nursing practice. In collaboration with the course lead instructor, the adjunct instructor assumes responsibility for assessing, planning, developing, implementing, and evaluating clinical and/or theoretical learning experiences. These experiences are designed in such a way as to facilitate critical thinking and foster student attainment of course objectives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Support of Student Learning Experiences: In collaboration with the lead instructor or director, assess, plan, develop, implement, and evaluate learning experiences designed to facilitate critical thinking and student attainment of course objectives. Participate in maintaining a collaborative learning environment in and out of the classroom, in the clinical setting, with departmental faculty members, and with clinical agencies. Department Responsibilities: Participate in maintaining a collaborative working relationship with departmental faculty members. Participate in establishing and implementing departmental goals and objectives. Communicate with lead instructor to remain current with program initiatives. Serve as a college representative in the clinical agency area. Participation in Nursing Faculty committees is encouraged and optional Desirable Qualifications To perform this job successfully, an individual must complete each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below represent the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Compensation Hourly; $50,025 to $69,173 (plus denominational benefits, depending upon qualifications and experience. Application Deadline Upon receipt of qualified candidate Apply for job PACIFIC UNION COLLEGE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER. Questions? Contact Human Resources Contact Us Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Phone: (707) 965-6231 Fax: (707) 965-6400 hr@puc.edu Employee Benefits Program Pacific Union College One Angwin Avenue Angwin, CA 94508 Campus Map (800) 862-7080 (707) 965-6313 Apply Give Contact Visit Careers Academics Useful Links Information Academic Departments Bookstore Calendar Campus Map Consumer Information Directory Disability Services Discrimination Policy Emergency Info Library News Online Programs Pay Student Bill Photo Gallery Privacy Policy PUC CARES Act Grant Records Office Student Planning Title IX Information For Who Are You? Current Students New Students Future Students Transfer Students Parents & Families Alumni Visitors Faculty & Staff Veterans © Copyright 2026. Pacific Union College. All Rights reserved. | Privacy policy"
